Z||000043||Eric||02-05-2001||09:31 PM||||I can't help thinking that there's someone out there who's having trouble with his clutch hydraulics, and he finds the thread on ATF when somebody directs him to the search function.  Point is, sometimes the knowledge gained on this forum is by trial and error.  God forbid someone finds the error thread first, and thinks that's the way to go.  Please, if there's any cluing-in to do, give em the hint before they screw themselves by way of our already debunked threads.||||reg||1
Z||000044||FieroJoe||02-05-2001||09:49 PM||||For sure!  I've used the search and found a myriad of info that really didnt pertain to what I was looking for, but good reading anyways.  A hint, "also check out a search on [insert keywords here]" following maybe even the smallest amount of info just to "get the ball rolling" on someones problem, in my opinion, would be a kind thing to do.  That way, you have at least got the questioning memeber started in the correct direction with whatever their problem is, and also gave them a few good keywords where they might also find what they are looking for.||||reg||1
